:: Widgets DoLX Changelog [widget]
<<widget "DoLXChangelog">>
	<div class="changelog-overlay">
		<div class="changelog-hero">
			<span class="changelog-hero-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128220;</span>
			<div>
				<div class="changelog-label">PATCH NOTES</div>
				<h1>DoL X-Change <span>v0.22.3</span></h1>
				<div class="changelog-apk-note"><strong>Official X-Change APK:</strong> Join the DoL Modding server and check the dedicated <a href="https://discord.com/channels/675158131688603721/1512272787572785162" target="_blank">X-Change Channel</a>.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<a class="changelog-release-link" href="https://gitgud.io/Akoz/dol-xchange/-/releases" target="_blank"><span aria-hidden="true">&#128279;</span> View the full changelog and all releases <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon new" aria-hidden="true">&#10022;</span> Changes and Additions</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Updated RBE to v0.6.2</strong> by <strong>Reiyu</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Added Bailey's Safe Word, a new Monogamy!Bailey coffee scene, and expanded the Monogamy!Bailey flat fight with its own dialogue.
			</li>
			<li>Updated Bailey's speech and fixed related interactions.
			</li>
			<li><strong>Add missing dialogue, toy reveals, Avery's responses, and correct rent, tax, deposit, and HBSC-debt checks while keeping existing DoLX content by D.N.A.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Rhythm to the Home Console</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Play a new rhythm game from the console at home or in Alex's cottage. Time taps, holds, drags, and simultaneous notes to a moving scan line.
			</li>
			<li>Each song has <strong>Easy</strong>, <strong>Normal</strong>, and <strong>Hard</strong> charts. Earn Perfect, Good, or Miss judgements and track score, accuracy, combo, grade, full combos, and all-Perfect clears. <strong>75% accuracy</strong> is needed to clear a chart.
			</li>
			<li>Includes <strong>eight built-in soundtrack songs</strong>, and supports uploaded music with automatically generated charts.
			</li>
			<li>Supports keyboard (six lanes with custom keybinds), mouse, and touch. Includes a seven-step tutorial, lane labels, reduced effects, pause/restart, and timing adjustments.
			</li>
			<li>Added a <strong>Rhythm Library</strong> for custom songs, charts, scores, and playlists. Make or edit charts, manage playlists, and import/export libraries as JSON. Exports do not contain audio files.
			</li>
			<li>Added <strong>13 challenges</strong>, <strong>11 achievements</strong>, and a daily challenge. Daily rewards are <strong>£200 Easy</strong>, <strong>£350 Normal</strong>, or <strong>£500 Hard</strong>, once per UTC day.
			</li>
			<li>Completing all regular challenges unlocks the Level 3 <strong>Rhythm Master</strong> feat. Custom or edited charts keep scores but cannot farm progression rewards.
			</li>
			<li>The interface and mobile controls have been improved. Other music pauses while playing and resumes when you leave.
			</li>
			<li>Fruit's draggable playfield also now ignores sidebar-swipe gestures during play.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Dragon Stars for Water Dragons</strong>
			<ul>
			<li><strong>Dragon Star</strong> is a rare six-pointed blue gem. The first <strong>Dragon Boost</strong> in a fight remains free; every extra Boost in that fight consumes one star.
			</li>
			<li>Stars can rarely be found while searching the nest shore and very rarely while combing the town beach.
			</li>
			<li>Stars appear next to pepper sprays in the sidebar, showing up to three slots and a <strong>+</strong> when more are held.
			</li>
			<li>Added a separate <strong>Dragon stars: Show / Hidden</strong> sidebar option and a Dragon Stars counter in the Cheat menu.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Ear Slime intrusive thoughts</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>New <strong>Ear slimes appear as intrusive thoughts</strong> setting lets hypnosis leave voices in your head instead of physical parasites, even with parasites disabled.
			</li>
			<li>A second hypnosis can add another voice. They still give commands, rewards, and punishments, but have no physical growth or chastity effects.
			</li>
			<li>Gwylan's <strong>Hypnotic Silence</strong> can temporarily quiet them; the sunken lake ruin altar removes them permanently.
			</li>
			<li>Related game text changes to match the setting.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Blindfold Adaptability</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Blindfolds are sold in the forest and sex toy shops and have their own wardrobe icon.
			</li>
			<li>Being blindfolded gives up to a <strong>30% chance to fail skill checks</strong>. Wearing one for seven days builds <strong>Adaptability</strong>, eventually removing the penalty. Progress fades while the blindfold is off.
			</li>
			<li>Certain transformations speed training, slow the loss, or reduce Stress. Acquired Insanity slowly reduces Trauma while blindfolded.
			</li>
			<li>At full Adaptability and <strong>50%+ Gwylan Love</strong>, ask Gwylan for <strong>Hypnotic Adaptability</strong>, which prevents progress fading while the hypnosis lasts.
			</li>
			<li>Teachers, students, Robin, and Kylar react to blindfolds at school. Strangers follow more often, but full Adaptability allows escape; high-Love Kylar may follow to protect you.
			</li>
			<li>The Traits panel shows Adaptability progress and the current skill-check penalty.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded Underground Brothel contracts and escape hunts</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Returning after a previous contract can lead to recognition and a <strong>three-day unpaid contract</strong> instead of being kept in a cell. This becomes more likely with more contract experience.
			</li>
			<li>Escaping previously can add <strong>five unpaid days</strong> to a newly signed contract.
			</li>
			<li>Breaking out of a contract can trigger a week of brothel hunters and corrupt police searching town and forest. Being caught means finishing the remaining contract plus five unpaid days.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Harper now offers weekly parasite requests</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>After selling Harper <strong>10 parasites</strong>, receive a weekly client request for a parasite species you've encountered, with a minimum activity level.
			</li>
			<li>A matching parasite earns <strong>4×, 6×, or 10×</strong> its usual price. Only one request can be completed per week.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Gwylan can remove Hypnotic Crossdressing</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>You can now ask Gwylan to weaken or remove the trait through hypnosis, rather than relying only on Harper.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added more Kylar interactions</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>At <strong>50+ Love</strong>, Kylar can take you on coffee dates from the park or arcade.
			</li>
			<li>There is also a <strong>25% daily chance</strong> for Kylar to visit during your café shift.
			</li>
			<li>Once Kylar's manor bedroom is unlocked, you can suggest going there instead of the orphanage when Kylar asks for somewhere private.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded Whitney's reactions to X-Change height changes</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Whitney may react to your new height at school <strong>once a week</strong>, with responses depending on Dominance and affection, including teasing, carrying, hugging, or intimidation.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded Robin's forest picnic</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Robin can breast drinking from the player during the milking scene when Robin's Dominance is suffecient or Lust is 60 or higher.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added rebellious orphans smoking in the loft</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>After buying cigarettes at the pub, sufficiently rebellious players have a <strong>25% chance</strong> to find orphans smoking in the loft, once daily between <strong>07:00 and 22:00</strong>. This does not use your cigarettes.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added full hygiene options to more bathrooms</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>The temple, brothel, strip club, and Seaspray Hotel bathrooms now support scooping, washing, brushing teeth, trimming nails, and grooming like the orphanage.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added new Heat/Rut Scream setting</strong>
			<ul>
			<li><strong>Can't Scream while in Heat/Rut</strong> removes the Scream action during heat or rut when enabled. <strong>Off by default</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>The Insanity <strong>Full Dissociation</strong> setting now warns clearly that it prevents screaming and fighting back.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Allure ignores fame setting</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Under <strong>Encounter Rate</strong>, use your full Allure for encounter checks instead of reducing most of it based on bad Fame.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>New keyboard shortcuts for minigames</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Wren's Blackjack now has <strong>Play at max bet</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>The pub dice game has <strong>Confirm max bet</strong> and <strong>Max out the stakes</strong> when a higher bet is possible.
			</li>
			<li>In the Fruit/Suika game, number keys activate powers; starting a mode now focuses the jar so arrow keys and Space work immediately.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Tweaks and Rebalancing</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Rebalanced Dragon Boost and pepper spray</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Dragon Boost now has a <strong>5% chance to instantly knock out</strong> its target. Other hits may glance off for light damage or miss.
			</li>
			<li>Pepper spray deals <strong>8% more damage</strong> and stuns targets for <strong>3 turns</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Drug-resistant enemies are stunned for <strong>1 turn</strong>. The Ivory Wraith is unaffected.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Clothing Dysphoria now develops over time</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Clothing Dysphoria builds <strong>hourly</strong> while an unaccepted style stays equipped, so tolerance can improve without repeatedly changing outfits.
			</li>
			<li>Updated the tooltip to explain the change.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Dysphoria is easier to recognise on screen</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Words and pronouns that cause Dysphoria, plus Dysphoria messages, now glow and move slightly. Comfortable words remain unchanged.
			</li>
			<li>Movement is disabled when reduced motion is requested.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Late slips now require actual lateness</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Leighton gives a late slip only after the player has been late <strong>twice in a week</strong>, rather than based on Delinquency alone.
			</li>
			<li>Bringing the slip to class excuses the lateness, avoiding an extra detention and Delinquency penalty.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated farm animal Respect</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Passive Respect loss is <strong>20% slower</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Pig Respect no longer passively drops to <strong>seeing you as fucktoy</strong>; encounters and actions can still lower it further. Other existing lower values remain.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated contraceptive pill and daily notifications</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Automatic contraceptive dosing now takes <strong>one pill per day</strong>, preventing overdoses.
			</li>
			<li>Daily-pill and X-Change spiking notifications now appear when they happen, rather than hours later.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Changed brothel virginity restoration</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Finishing all five trials now lifts the Purity cap back to the virgin maximum <strong>without resetting current Purity</strong> or undoing existing corruption.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated body and clothing comfort</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Sleepwear no longer causes Arousal from rubbing sensitive nipples or genitals; underwear worn beneath it still can.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed rubbing text mentioning clothing already removed.
			</li>
			<li>Chest binders now affect breast insecurity based on how the chest looks while dressed: flattening can prevent big-breast insecurity but may create small-breast insecurity. Exposed breast size still matters.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Water Dragon activities</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Moonstones and black pearls can be found by combing the <strong>island beach</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Returning as a Water Dragon no longer gives the same spear again.
			</li>
			<li>Docile assessments and daily brooding now increase Harper's affection in the Pelagos badend.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Improved other gameplay interactions</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Consenting to plant people now requires <strong>Deviancy 2</strong> instead of 3.
			</li>
			<li>Sex during Gwylan's ritual increases Deviancy; Dryad Nectar collected there counts for Gwylan's current request, without exceeding the requested amount.
			</li>
			<li>Praying at the temple counts as a short rest and reduces Autism Load, while off-focus Willpower training still has its normal cost.
			</li>
			<li><strong>Aquatic Lungs</strong> bypasses swimming checks and breath-holding text in Winter's ducking-stool demonstration.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Made combat difficulty labels clearer</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Actions that can fail because the body does not obey now show labels such as <strong>Pull away (Challenging)</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Labels respect difficulty-visibility settings; success chances are unchanged.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated the classroom blackmail task</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>The empty-classroom masturbation task now completes on orgasm, not after five uninterrupted minutes.
			</li>
			<li>Being interrupted after finishing no longer fails it, and merely standing naked does not complete it.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Changed antique selling</strong>
			<ul>
			<li><strong>Sell antiques</strong> now keeps the <strong>Ivory Necklace</strong>. A separate <strong>Sell the ivory necklace</strong> option lets you choose whether to give up its payout bonuses and story consequences.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Fixes and Improvements</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Fixed save loading, settings, and character data</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Older saves can recover missing gameplay settings and invalid <strong>NaN</strong> values affecting Allure and pregnancy chances.
			</li>
			<li>Compatibility checks now run after the incoming save has loaded.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed older transformed-body shapes, genital-size conversion, and empty or incomplete body caches without resetting player progress.
			</li>
			<li>Corrected setting and price values, and fixed Settings exports overflowing smaller phone screens.
			</li>
			<li>Preserved character, sensitivity, Identity, and system settings during transfers, plus disabled options when saving new-game defaults.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed misleading import warnings and Poppy settings on older saves.
			</li>
			<li>Feat hints now stay open after tapping on mobile.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed pregnancy data, births, and Water Dragon eggs</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Nest setup now runs after pregnancy stats exist; skin-colour conversion safely checks both pregnancy slots.
			</li>
			<li>Water Dragons with Harpy wings, including Melusine chimeras, now lay <strong>Water Dragon eggs</strong>, not Harpy eggs. Affected saves repair after the next in-game day.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed birth scenes with <strong>four or more babies</strong>, including baby counts, cradling, and aftercare text.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed the GooseFem womb tattoo moving off-centre during pregnancy.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed pregnancy clothing sprites</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>School shirts, pyjama shirts, and dress shirts no longer vanish during pregnancy.
			</li>
			<li>Belly and outfit changes no longer create duplicate clothing or stale clipping, and portrait clothing stays intact.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed NPC gender recognition and pronouns</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>NPCs recognise the player's preferred gender once told they are trans or after sufficient Love, rather than automatically after seeing them naked.
			</li>
			<li>The setting for recognising gender when naked now works correctly.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed Briar's pronouns, Robin's crossdressing pronouns, Whitney's restraint aftermath pronouns, and an undefined-pronoun error at the Brothel virginity auction.
			</li>
			<li>Robin's gender conversations now respect school and bedtime circumstances.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed gender-based crowd Dysphoria counting Love Interests, Gwylan, or Mickey incorrectly. At least two other qualifying NPCs are still needed.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Gwylan clothing requests and conversations</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>New and existing clothing requests now recognise the correct slots, including outfits, and respect hypnosis restrictions on modded clothing.
			</li>
			<li>Older broken requests are repaired where possible, while missing clothing is handled safely without affecting unrelated items.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed an error after asking Gwylan about the Ivory Wraith brand and corrected available options for the relationship.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed Gwylan's hide-and-seek error after furniture falls on them, which could leave characters stuck.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Colosseum breeding</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Opponent climax or defeat no longer automatically ends the breeding scene.
			</li>
			<li>Added <strong>End breeding → Stop</strong> to the combat menu.
			</li>
			<li>Stopping before the player's first climax causes a permanent ban.
			</li>
			<li>Pregnancy is no longer forced before the player climaxes.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed World Override confirmation</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>The risk-confirmation checkbox now works whenever World Override is opened, not only after a version update.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed the mirror and tattoo menus</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>If a saved bodywriting category is no longer available, the menu returns to <strong>General</strong> instead of giving an error.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed combat and orgasm-state errors</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Passing the Willpower check now prevents both the stun and orgasm when <strong>You cum even if you resist the stun</strong> is unchecked.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed an <strong>orgasmcurrent</strong> error after Water Dragon egg-laying or being carried away by a slime in the old sewers.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed attackers continuing sex actions after running off with the player's clothes; they now let go before fleeing.
			</li>
			<li>Sex with Bailey no longer incorrectly raises Sex Fame.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Avery's events and clothing checks</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>The party choice now says <strong>brown fox</strong> instead of naming Gwylan too early.
			</li>
			<li>Purple-pill herms are no longer incorrectly rejected from Avery's dates.
			</li>
			<li>Cold baths are now available at Avery's mansion.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed shop and clothing-event issues</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Being caught at a shopping-centre register now leaves the player on <strong>High Street</strong>; the school-library register leaves them on <strong>Oxford Street</strong>, not Domus Street.
			</li>
			<li>Jacket removal options now show the jacket's name instead of <strong>naked</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>The park underwear-running blackmail task now checks that outer clothing has been removed.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed animal clothing encounters</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Animals no longer bite a naked player incorrectly or fail to grab underwear after outer clothes are removed.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Alex dialogue</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Alex no longer stays silent during sex when no special line applies.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed farm machinery and clearing</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Fixed invalid clearing times and Fatigue when a loader was enabled without a tractor.
			</li>
			<li>Other attachments now require a tractor, and water-field excavation progress text is corrected.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon images" aria-hidden="true">&#10024;</span> Art and Graphics</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Improved Virtual Pet minigame art</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Aoki Utage pet snake art</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Fem pet snake drawn by <strong>Estalia</strong> and edited by <strong>χø£¡ϯԋ</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Added an <strong>Aoki Utage Water Dragon</strong> by <strong>χø£¡ϯԋ</strong>.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated GooseMasc art</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Added pet snake graphics by <strong>kitbullz</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Added <strong>Okami</strong> transformation artwork by <strong>VViktor (Vvikz0)</strong>.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated GooseFem art</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Added <strong>Modded Face 28</strong> by <strong>Marin</strong>
			</li>
			<li>Added <strong>Modded Face 29</strong> by <strong>sussyorenji</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Added pet snake artwork by <strong>Estalia</strong>.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
<</widget>>
